From 86e08fc769c718357ab3f8621f7c920945cb44a1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tunkoal <tunkoal@163.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 18:11:39 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] apn: allow devices to supply their own APN installation

The Rothko build on LineageOS 24 fails in Kati because the common APN
prebuilt and the device prebuilt both emit Product/etc/apns-conf.xml
install recipes. LOCAL_OVERRIDES_MODULES filters package selection later
and cannot remove the already emitted duplicate recipe.

Add the opt-in lineage_apn.use_device_apns boolean on the owning common
prebuilt. Unset/false retains the common module. True disables its Soong
install actions while the device supplies its own table and overrides.

Base: 2842825e44b5ad6e247467bd7a16c1d8bf80407f
Evidence and alternatives: Rothko bringup/phase-b/
TELECOM_BROADNET_20261115.zh-CN.md, install-rule follow-up.
The current vendor APN module has no configurable device replacement
entry point. Make filtering alone reproduced the duplicate-rule failure,
and prebuilt_etc does not implement source/prebuilt preference selection.
Device XML, its installation module and runtime Provider remain device
and existing framework responsibilities. No device identity is hardcoded.

Checks passed: bpfmt syntax/format, whitespace, actual Make bool typing
for true/false/empty and stock-table SHA-256. Complete installation graph,
unified images and actual Telecom/Broadnet SIM acceptance are pending.

Change-Id: I378b31671a17c0ffaae511791aa3300d126ceb31
---
 Android.bp | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Android.bp b/Android.bp
index 5b2cb8d..51afdc9 100644
--- a/Android.bp
+++ b/Android.bp
@@ -29,6 +29,10 @@ filegroup {
 
 prebuilt_etc_xml {
     name: "apns-conf.xml",
+    enabled: select(soong_config_variable("lineage_apn", "use_device_apns"), {
+        true: false,
+        default: true,
+    }),
     product_specific: true,
     src: ":apns-conf",
     schema: ":apns-conf-schema",

base-commit: 2842825e44b5ad6e247467bd7a16c1d8bf80407f
